<BaseLayout title="About Seller Operations Lab" description="The scope, editorial responsibility, sources, and limitations behind Seller Operations Lab product-image guides and browser tools." activeNav="/about/">
  <section class="legal-hero legal-shell"><p class="eyebrow">SELLER OPERATIONS LAB</p><h1>About the project</h1><p>Product-image workflows and browser tools for independent online sellers.</p></section>
  <section class="legal-content legal-shell">
    <h2>Scope and editorial responsibility</h2>
    <p>Seller Operations Lab is the editorial and software identity responsible for this site's guides, marketplace references and browser tools. The project focuses on preparing, inspecting and comparing product-image files before online publication. It is not an Etsy or Shopify integration, retouching suite or marketplace-management service.</p>
    <p>Technical guides and software may be developed with AI assistance. Platform-specific claims are linked to official documentation; workflow recommendations, measurements and calculations are identified separately with their methods and limitations. The project does not claim firsthand seller experience, sales results or professional photography credentials.</p>
    <p>The project currently uses <strong>damaheritage.com</strong> as its technical home; Seller Operations Lab is the current editorial identity on that domain. The domain and project are independent of Etsy, Shopify and Google.</p>
    <h2>What the tools do</h2>
    <p>The tools process selected images in your browser and do not upload them to this site. They create technical checks and exports; they do not guarantee platform acceptance, image quality, search placement or sales. Keep your original files and review the final listing in the destination platform.</p>
    <h2>Funding and independence</h2>
    <p>The tools are free to use. The site may seek advertising support, but the current version does not load advertising or analytics scripts. Each marketplace reference displays the date its official source was last checked. If a source-backed claim is found to be wrong, the project will correct the text and its review date; no response-time promise is made. The public <a href="/contact/">correction tracker</a> is the contact channel; there is currently no private support inbox.</p>
    <p><a href="/methodology/">Read the methodology</a> or <a href="/contact/">report a correction</a>.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
